Hi,

I still can't believe it. More than a year after my first game, I finally 
ascended. And this was with my first character ever to enter the Valley !

Just in case : there are spoilers after this line.

So... I started this game two weeks ago, during the Full Moon. I got a co-
aligned altar and two bags of tricks in Minetown. After I got the 
luckstone, a lot of sacrifices gave me Snickersnee and very high luck. 
Another altar (converted) at dlvl 7 crowns me the Hand of Elbereth, and 
Oracle at dlvl 9 gave me useful hints. Dlvl 10 was a Big Room, with 
upstairs to Sokoban (from where I got an amulet of reflection). I made the 
mines before sokoban in this game, because the Big Room was filled with 
angry monsters and I could not deal with all of them at this time.

Somewhere in the mines I got a wand of polymorph, and used it on a lot of 
stuff to get some useful items : a magic marker (the only one I got in 
this game !) and some useful rings (levitation, conflict), scrolls and 
wands.

At dlvl 13 was the first polymorph trap. I put a boulder on top of it, but 
a homonculus managed to step on it (don't know how, there was a boulder on 
top ?!) and polymorphed to... an arch-lich. Goodbye blessed +2 dwarvish 
roundshield :( Some items were cursed, but the arch-lich paid for that.

Fort Ludios portal was on dlvl 15. At this time I was two weaponing 
Snickersnee and my original katana, and wearing a ring of conflict, so 
this map was easy. Killing a silver dragon leaves me silver scales, soon 
silver scale mail. After what I swapped my amulet of reflection for an 
amulet of life changing.

The quest was on dlvl 16. After Ashikaga Takauji woke up (heh, I am 
Lawful) I threw a potion of paralysis to him, and stabbed him to death. I 
did not use the Tsurigi of Muramasa in this game, as I wanted to try two 
weaponing. I originally planned Grayswandir and a silver saber, but I did 
not get Grayswandir. Maybe in another game...

On dlvl 17 there was a temple (cross aligned, but I bought protection with 
Croesus' loot). After an identification session, I read a scroll of 
genocide and wiped out master mind flayers. A blessed one, written with my 
magic marker, wiped out all L.

Dlvl 18 was the rogue level, a Barrow Wight gave me a long sword. At dlvl 
20 was a fountain, so I finally got Excalibur and enchanted it to +6. 
Goodbye Snickersnee...

Somewhere between the rogue level and the castle I got a silver saber from 
a sergeant or lieutenant, which I enchanted quickly to +6. Now two 
weaponing was deadly, very few monsters did survive the first two hits (I 
was also very fast, as I got a pair of speed boots in a general store).

The Castle was at dlvl 29. I zapped a wand of striking to get rid of the 
drawbridge, and wished for some stuff :

- 2 blessed scrolls of charging, got one
- a blessed bag of holding, got it (the only one I got in the game !)
- a blessed +3 cloak of magic resistance, got it (the last item I really 
needed to survive)

(read the scroll of charging I got with my first wish)

- a blessed +3 T-shirt, got it (I found an Hawaiian shirt shortly after, 
cruel RNG...)
- 2 blessed scrolls of charging, got one

(no charges left)

After these wishes I made some holy water, charged my magic marker, 
enchanted/{rust,fire}proofed my stuff and prepare myself to enter the 
underworld for the first time. If I had known, I would have keep more 
potion of sake/confusion, by the way...

The Valley was easy, but the succession of mazes of Gehennom was tedious. 
Mazes levels are a very good idea, but I did not imagine Hell like this. 
Asmodeus, Juiblex, Baalzebub were no problem, Orcus was hit by a potion of 
paralysis, died quickly and was kind enough to give me a wand of death 
full of charges.

And here come the first human error (never play when tired) : at this time 
(dlvl 41, before entering Vlad's tower) I needed to BUC test some items, 
make holy water and use scrolls/wands of create monster to sacrifice. So I 
returned to dlvl 17 (were was my stash) and used the altar, which was 
cross aligned. So when praying to get holy water... I got unholy water and 
angered my goddess. That was plain stupidity, but I managed to do more 
stupid : I converted the altar... with the priest nearby ! So I had to 
kill him, loosing my telepathy (but one of the helmets I wanted to 
identify was a helm of telepathy, lucky me) and being a murderer. But I 
bought all my protection from this priest, so I got all my gold back. A 
lot of sacrifices after that I got Frost Brand. After some more sacrifices 
to reset my prayer timeout I got back to Minetown to get the candles and 
buy some protection from the priest, and returned to dlvl 41 where Vlad 
was waiting. Vlad was no problem, and I found Fire Brand in his tower.

The Wizard was waiting at dlvl 42 (that's a sign). I knew I need to find 
the vibrating square to perform the ritual, so I did not enter his tower 
until I found it (at dlvl 49). Before fighting the wizard I wiped out 
all ; because I did not know he wizard had his own private room, and I 
wanted to prevent a stupid death while fighting him. After what I did the 
ritual, entering Moloch's Sanctum for an epic battle. After I got the 
Amulet, the game was just zapping wands of teleportation (I had a lot of 
wands in my bag of holding !) and killing the wizard, again and again. 
After he summonned minions and cursed my bag of holding I zapped a wand of 
death to him each time he appeared and genocided the mind flayers, just in 
case.

I did enter the planes, killing the Wizard and avoiding creatures. Plane 
of air was the most challenging, as I had nothing to detect the portal and 
there were powerful monsters. I finally made my way to the plane of fire, 
were I sank in lava. Tried to walk out, did not work. Zapped a wand of 
cold, did not work. Finally I broke the wand of cold, and used my pick axe 
to get away of this place. In this plane the Wizard was very challenging, 
I had only 96HP after one of our fights (all my wands of death were empty, 
sadly).

Finally in the Astral Plane, I was welcomed by four angels of Amaterasu 
Omikami. But I had a ring of conflict, so they turned hostile. After 
killing them I spent some time to be unburdened, and drop most of my 
artifacts and objects. I should have done this before, of course. 
Pestilence, Death and Famine were easy (though I had a moment of panic 
when ill and only had cursed potions of full healing, but my blessed 
unicorn horn saved me), and the good temple was the last one I tried.

For the little story I was ill at eight squares of the good altar.

And now, the (manual) dump... Manual because I did not install the dump 
patch. By the way all of this was on a vanilla nethack 3.4.3 with eight 
patches : four patches from Patric Mueller (the ones fixing crashes), 
menucolors/showbuc, statuscolors and use_darkgray.

The voice of Amaterasu Omikami booms: "Congratulations, mortal!"--More--

